  "recent_corrections": [
    {
      "ts": "2026-08-05T01:41:20.517203+00:00",
      "text": "A recent WATCH-level flag was wrong: a story about Latvia sending about 20 soldiers to the Strait of Hormuz was mistakenly flagged as a Baltic security signal. This one was a genuine deployment, not a keyword-matching error like the wildfire correction below \u2014 but it's Latvia's own contribution to an international coalition maritime security mission on the other side of the world, with no connection to Russia or the Baltic region. The scoring gap that let this through (a Baltic country's own unrelated foreign deployments passing as a Baltic security signal) has been fixed. As always, the false positive stays in the historical record rather than being quietly deleted.",
      "context": "Latvia plans to send about 20 soldiers to Strait of Hormuz \u2014 flagged WATCH, 2026-08-04"
    },
    {
      "ts": "2026-08-04T20:45:44.779097+00:00",
      "text": "A recent WATCH-level flag was wrong: a story about Lithuania sending firefighters to help France fight wildfires was mistakenly flagged as a Baltic security signal. Cause: a scoring bug \u2014 generic words like 'deployed' and 'reinforcements' (meant to catch real troop movements) were also matching ordinary disaster-response language. That bug, and several similar ones found in a full audit of the scoring keywords, has been fixed. The false positive stays in the historical record below rather than being quietly deleted \u2014 see our policy on this.",
      "context": "Lithuania sends 32 firefighters to help France fight wildfires \u2014 flagged WATCH, 2026-08-01"
    }
  ],
  "recent_updates": [
    {
      "ts": "2026-09-01T19:06:18.290547+00:00",
      "title": "New: faster early warning between full scans",
      "text": "The full 150-source sweep takes about 19 minutes, so it can only run six times a day -- meaning up to 9.5 hours could pass between looks. A new lightweight check now runs every 2 hours over the direct publisher feeds (ERR, LSM, Delfi, Postimees, Yle and others) and raises an early warning if something real appears. It stays completely silent otherwise."
    },
    {
      "ts": "2026-09-01T18:59:36.432424+00:00",
      "title": "Fewer, better alerts",
      "text": "Reviewing every alert ever sent found many were reassuring news (\"officials say no attack is coming\"), scenario/analysis pieces, or the same story repeating for days. Those are now shown as context instead of arriving as an alert. Replayed over the full history this removes about half the notifications while keeping every genuine incident."
    },
    {
      "ts": "2026-09-01T18:59:36.432420+00:00",
      "title": "New: direct publisher feeds for resilience",
      "text": "Until now every tracked source was reached through Google News, which has occasionally blocked the whole scan at once. The monitor now also reads 15 feeds straight from the publishers themselves -- ERR, LSM, Delfi, Postimees, Yle, Meduza and others -- so a Google outage no longer means a blind spot. They are also far faster to fetch."
    },
    {
      "ts": "2026-09-01T18:59:36.432391+00:00",
      "title": "Fixed: one source could trigger a WARN on its own",
      "text": "WARN is supposed to mean several independent sources report the same thing. A configuration quirk let a single organisation listed under two tiers score as its own corroboration. Confirmation is now counted per organisation, not per feed, so WARN means what it says."
    },
    {
      "ts": "2026-08-30T20:31:19.899514+00:00",
      "title": "Fixed: NATO training near Kaliningrad going uncaught",
      "text": "A real NATO exercise near Kaliningrad was not flagged because the relevance filter only matched the literal phrase \"military exercise\" -- most outlets actually write \"drills\"/\"wargames\"/\"manoeuvres\" instead. Added coverage for those terms (gated on military context where the bare word has an everyday meaning too), so this class of story is caught going forward."
    },
    {
      "ts": "2026-08-24T08:05:24.483648+00:00",
      "title": "New: power grid outages charted on the public site",
      "text": "The forced (unplanned) generation-unit outage data /gridoutage already fetches from ENTSO-E is now also recorded every scan and charted on the site -- a new \"Power grid outages over time\" trend alongside GPS-jamming, AIS, military aircraft, and thermal hotspots. Still informational only, same as /gridoutage always was."
    },
    {
      "ts": "2026-08-23T10:36:00.918265+00:00",
      "title": "New: weekly public summary on Mastodon/Bluesky/Discord",
      "text": "A once-a-week summary post (quiet/watch/warn counts, latest escalation index reading) to the public Mastodon/Bluesky/Discord accounts only -- deliberately never Telegram, since that channel's QUIET-suppression rule stays untouched. Keeps the public accounts visibly active during long quiet stretches."
    },
    {
      "ts": "2026-08-23T10:31:13.597356+00:00",
      "title": "New: AIS kinematic-anomaly detection",
      "text": "Flags a vessel whose two recorded AIS positions imply a physically impossible speed (a classic GPS-spoofing tell, though also possibly a transponder misreport) -- private chat only, informational, never part of scoring or public alerting. Deliberately does NOT flag a vessel simply not reappearing in a later scan, since AIS coverage is already a short, non-exhaustive window."
    },
    {
      "ts": "2026-08-23T10:21:06.550779+00:00",
      "title": "New: downloadable CSV history export",
      "text": "Two new downloads on the site: scan-level history (level, source counts per scan) and the Composite Escalation Index (deviation score per scan), as CSV, for anyone doing independent analysis of this project's own data."
    },
    {
      "ts": "2026-08-23T10:14:00.564156+00:00",
      "title": "New: Discord as a fifth public alert channel",
      "text": "WATCH/WARN and recovery alerts now also post to Discord via an incoming webhook -- same infrequent, Telegram-independent scope as Mastodon and Bluesky. Requires a free DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL once the owner sets one up."
    },
    {
